        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Florida, New Jersey, Lake Okeechobee, Miami River, downtown Miami, Clifton, Passaic, Passaic County, Lake Harbor\n- Systems: Miami Canal, C-6 Canal, Dundee Canal\n- Concepts: industrial canals, hydropower, manufacturing\n\nFacts:\n- The Miami Canal, also called the C-6 Canal, flows from Lake Okeechobee in Florida to its terminus at the Miami River, which flows through downtown Miami.\n- Lake Harbor is located along the southern banks of Lake Okeechobee at the beginning of the Miami Canal.\n- The Dundee Canal was an industrial canal in Clifton and Passaic in Passaic County, New Jersey.\n- The Dundee Canal supplied hydropower and water for manufacturing.",
